</section>
<h2>HERE'S WHAT CONCERNS ME MOST.</h2>
<p>These reports and proposed decisions are on the consent calendar.</p>
<p>For anyone unfamiliar, that's where several agenda items can be approved together in one vote, often without individual discussion unless someone asks to pull an item.</p>
<p>Think of it like agreeing to pay the restaurant bill before looking at the receipt.</p>
<p>Maybe every charge is correct.</p>
<p>But wouldn't you want to check?</p>
<p>I'm not claiming anyone has done anything wrong.</p>
<p>I'm asking whether the City's spending, contract decisions, and oversight are being explained well enough for residents to understand what's happening.</p>
<p>That's why I started StayJustIn.</p>
<p>📍 West Covina City Council Meeting — TONIGHT, Tuesday, November 17, at 7 PM at City Hall.</p>
<p>I've put together a more detailed breakdown of the financial report, the traffic project, Kimley-Horn's previous City work, and the questions I believe deserve answers.</p>
<p>Read more at StayJustIn.com before tonight's meeting.</p>
<p>And I'd really like to hear what my neighbors think.</p>
<p>Should Council pull the financial report and the Kimley-Horn contract from the consent calendar so these questions can be discussed publicly?</p>
<p>Or do you feel comfortable with the information that's already been provided?</p>
<p>I'm interested in hearing both sides. You don't have to agree with my concerns, but I think we should all be able to explain why we support or question these decisions.</p>
<p>Because whether we're praising City Hall or holding it accountable, we should be working from the same facts.</p>
<p>Stay informed. Stay involved. StayJustIn.</p>

